{"seq": 1550, "kind": "worker:tool_update", "line": "[tool in_progress] git commit -m \"obs: port the deployed fleet delta (argv store form, lease fallback, honesty demotion, titles)\n\nPort the four live-verified fixes from the deployed collector onto main's\nrizzstack-observability collector, RED-first (tests were written first and\nfailed on main's collector):\n\n1. FLEET CLI ARGV: default_fleet_argv knows the real subcommands'\n   --state-dir DIR form (bundlebees attempts|status --state-dir DIR); the\n   historical attempt op=... shape never existed (fleet_command_failed\n   root cause). The store is appended only for callers that pass one, so\n   the pinned bare two-read-only-calls contract stays intact.\n2. FLEET ROWS: fleet_section prefers the CLI source and falls back to the\n   dispatch-lease store (state_dir/leases/att_*.json, newest 24) joined\n   with the outbox's bee-landed terminal states; fallback rows carry\n   branch/model/title. The CLI always wins when it answers and the\n   fallback never invents a bee_cap from the stale store config.\n3. FLEET HONESTY: ACTIVE-state rows whose last heartbeat is older than\n   the staleness threshold demote to unknown and are NOT counted\n   in-flight (the attempt store never records terminal states; counting\n   them reported an inflated 203 against a real 3).\n4. JOB/TASK TITLES: pipeline_section emits the job title+summary from the\n   goal and each task title from the first acceptance-criterion\n   statement, scrubbed; absent fields stay null.\n\nThe snapshot schema gains the optional model/title/summary row fields\nunder the existing no-bump extension convention (old documents keep\nvalidating). The bottlenecks section and the job-envelope unwrap from\nmerged #42 are preserved untouched.\" && git log --oneline -2", "stop_reason": null, "text": null, "lseq": 1564, "ts": 1794874662.3842049}
